{title: 637 - Son of God, Eternal Savior}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #637 • IN BABILONE • 8.7.8.7.D.}
{lyricist: Somerset C. Lowry}
{composer: Dutch folk tune}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 637}
{meta: tune IN BABILONE}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.7.D.}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Son [Am]of God, [Bm]eternal [D]Savior,
[Am]Source of [D]life and [Bm]truth [C]and grace,
[D]Work made flesh, whose [G]birth [Am]among [Bm]us
[C]Hallows [D]all our human [Em]race,
[Am]You [D]our head, [C]who throned [D]in glory,
[Em]For Your [Dm]own will ever [G/D]plead:
[Am/E]Fill [Em]us [Am]with Your [D]love [D7/C]and pity,
[D/F#]Heal our [G]wrongs, and help [Am]our [D]need.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Bind [Am]us all [Bm]as [C]one [D]together
[Am]In [D]Your church's [Bm]sacred [C]fold,
[D]Weak and healthy, [G]poor [Am]and wealthy,
[C]Sad and [D]joyful, young [B/D#]and [Em]old.
[Am]Is [D]there want [C]or pain [D]or sorrow?
[Em]Make us [Dm]all the burden [G/D]share.
[Am/E]Are [Em]there [Am]spirits [D]crushed [D7/C]and broken?
[D/F#]Teach us, [G]Lord, to soothe [Am]their [D]care.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]As [Am]You, Lord, [Bm]have [C]lived [D]for others,
[Am]So may [D]we for [Bm]others [C]live.
[D]Freely have Your [G]gifts [Am]been granted;
[C]Freely [D]may Your servants [Em]give.
[Am]Yours [D]the gold [C]and Yours [D]the silver,
[Em]Yours the [Dm]wealth of land [C]and [G/D]sea;
[Am/E]We [Em]but [Am]stewards [D]of [D7/C]Your bounty
[D/F#]Held in [G]solemn trust [Am]will [D]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Come, [Am]O Christ, [Bm]and [C]reign [D]among [G]us,
[Am]King of [D]love and [Bm]Prince [C]of Peace;
[D]Hush the storm of [G]strife [Am]and passion,
[C]Bid its [D]cruel discords [Em]cease.
[Am]By [D]Your patient [C]years [D]of toiling,
[Em]By Your [Dm]silent hours [C]of [G/D]pain,
[Am/E]Quench [Em]our [Am]fevered [D]thirst [D7/C]of pleasure,
[D/F#]Stem our [G]selfish greed [Am]of [D]gain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Son [Am]of God, [Bm]eternal [D]Savior,
[Am]Source of [D]life and [Bm]truth [C]and grace,
[D]Word made flesh, whose [G]birth [Am]among [Bm]us
[C]Hallows [D]all our human [Em]race:
[Am]By [D]Your [Bm]praying, [C]by [D]Your willing
[Em]That Your [Dm]people should [C]be [G/D]one,
[Am/E]Grant, [Em]oh, [Am]grant our [D]hope's [D7/C]fruition:
[D/F#]Here on [G]earth Your will [Am]be [D]done.
{end_of_verse}
